The proliferation of seismic attributes is associated with the period starting from the mid-1960s, as indicated by the contributions from Milo Backus and Bill Schneider, and the development of the velocity spectrum by Tury Taner and Fulton Koehler. This period also saw the emergence of multifold data aiding interval velocity computations. Source: gsgpy_70_5_3SO.pdf — page 4.

